luation panel displaying BM25 metrics and expected values. I plan to also include a command/artifact drawer with the exact Anserini commands and output previews. Users will be able to type a query or click on sample queries to initiate a live search. End-to-end verification will be performed, including browser tests.\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tf4vcaf2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p ./.pi-bench-rewrites"},"thoughtSignature":""}],"api":"google-generative-ai","provider":"google","model":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","usage":{"input":5189,"output":2018,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":7207,"cost":{"input":0.010378,"output":0.024216,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.034594}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780602994642,"responseId":"ctghapP6LdS11MkPya-VuAw"}},"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Reframing Task Instructions**\n\nI'm currently working on rewriting the task instructions. My goal is to maintain complete technical accuracy and detail in a neutral tone. I'm focusing on preserving all of the original requirements and details, including setup, dependencies, commands, file names, and acceptance criteria. The rewritten Product Requirements Document (PRD) will be saved to `./.pi-bench-rew`.\n\n\n**Defining Application Purpose**\n\nI'm now clarifying the application's core function. It's to be a diagnostic workbench, specifically for live retrieval on NFCorpus, and will be a containerized web app deployable on Render. This means focusing on Anserini setup, live searching, BM25 evaluation against expected metrics, and clear display of commands and results. The project scope is limited to NFCorpus, avoiding the broader BEIR dashboard concept.\n\n\n**Clarifying Project Objectives**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on defining project constraints. I'm focusing on the integration of live search with Anserini. Specifically, I plan to leverage local Anserini knowledge and the existing repo as the main source for 